<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Have You Met Miss Jones" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1937
Composer:	Richard Rodgers
Lyricist:	Lorenz Hart
Form:	32-bar AABA
Key:	F major

“Have You Met Miss Jones?” was written for the
Broadway musical I’d Rather Be Right, which premiered
in 1937. Its bridge is notable for moving through
major-third-related key centers, a harmonic idea later
associated with John Coltrane’s “Giant Steps” and
“Countdown.”</spComments>
